---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, GITHUB_ORG } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Contact"
  description="How to reach BabelStacks."
>
  <section class="wrap page">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1 class="page-title">Contact</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We are in early development and reading everything that comes in.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        <a class="email" href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Code</h2>
      <p>
        Repositories and issue trackers live at
        <a href={GITHUB_ORG} rel="noopener">github.com/BabelStacks</a>. For
        anything about a specific tool, an issue there is usually faster than
        email.
      </p>

      <h2>What is useful to include</h2>
      <p>
        If you are writing about a possible collaboration or a problem in your
        own work, these help us give a straight answer:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The material — what it is, roughly how much, and its current form</li>
        <li>What you are trying to do with it that you currently cannot</li>
        <li>Any constraints: licensing, access restrictions, deadlines</li>
      </ul>
      <p>A rough description is fine. We would rather hear early than polished.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .email {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
</style>
